From 9b8b4aa10affcb682b0998b7f10cfca084701fb3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jesse Casco <jesse.casco@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 19:30:40 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 160/161] media: qcom: camss: x1e80100: Drop CSID2

CAMSS assumes that CSID n feeds VFE n: csid_set_power() powers the VFE
with the CSID's index, camss_buf_done() completes buffers on the VFE
with the CSID's index, and camss_reg_update() updates the CSID with the
VFE's index.

X1E80100 lists three full CSIDs but only two full VFEs, so the lite
CSIDs sit one index above their VFEs:

  CSID:  0, 1, 2, LITE0 (3), LITE1 (4)
  VFE:   0, 1, LITE0 (2), LITE1 (3)

CSID_LITE0 powers VFE_LITE1, and CSID_LITE1 fails to stream with
"Failed to power up pipeline: -22" because there is no VFE 4. CSID2 has
no VFE of its own, so nothing can use it.

Drop CSID2 from the resources. The lite CSIDs move to indices 2 and 3,
matching their VFEs, and every CSID feeds the VFE with its index again.
X1E80100 is the only SoC without an ISPIF whose CSID and VFE lists
didn't line up.

The lite CSID entities become msm_csid2 and msm_csid3 instead of
msm_csid3 and msm_csid4. The CSID index is also the
CSID_TOP_IO_PATH_CFG0() slot each CSID programs, so the lite CSIDs now
use slots 2 and 3.

Fixes: 1830cf0f56c3 ("media: qcom: camss: Add x1e80100 specific support")
Suggested-by: Gjorgji Rosikopulos <gjorgji.rosikopulos@oss.qualcomm.com>
Signed-off-by: Jesse Casco <jesse.casco@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss.c | 20 --------------------
 1 file changed, 20 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss.c b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss.c
index 1aa8a0545..51814a74f 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss.c
@@ -4347,26 +4347,6 @@ static const struct camss_subdev_resources csid_res_x1e80100[] = {
 			.formats = &csid_formats_gen2
 		},
 	},
-	/* CSID2 */
-	{
-		.regulators = {},
-		.clock = { "gcc_axi_hf", "gcc_axi_sf", "cpas_ahb",
-			   "cpas_fast_ahb", "csid", "csid_csiphy_rx" },
-		.clock_rate = { { 0 },
-				{ 0 },
-				{ 64000000, 80000000 },
-				{ 80000000,  100000000, 200000000,
-				  300000000, 400000000 },
-				{ 300000000, 400000000, 480000000 },
-				{ 300000000, 400000000, 480000000 }, },
-		.reg = { "csid2" },
-		.interrupt = { "csid2" },
-		.csid = {
-			.hw_ops = &csid_ops_680,
-			.parent_dev_ops = &vfe_parent_dev_ops,
-			.formats = &csid_formats_gen2
-		},
-	},
 	/* CSID_LITE0 */
 	{
 		.regulators = {},
